h under $100,000 in the bank. No public general-election polling is available, so the picture rests on fundamentals and expert assessments.\n\nRaters broadly place the race in solid-to-likely Republican territory, with five of ten calling it Solid or Safe Republican and only one rating it Lean Republican. Prediction markets give Halpin roughly a one-in-seven chance. The Democratic-leaning national midterm environment offers some counterweight, and Halpin's long history in Suffolk County politics gives him name recognition, but Garbarino's incumbency, fundraising, and the district's lean make him a clear favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0904, "margin": -8.3}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1051, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1048, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0688, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0718, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.079, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0871, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.121, "margin": -8.2}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1129, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0872, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0882, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0842, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.118, "margin": -8.0}]}